@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<div class="about-container" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 1rem;">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">About This App</h1>

    <p class="mb-4">
        This is a personal book tracking application built to help you organize, manage, and reflect on your reading habits. Whether you're an avid reader or just trying to finish that one book on your shelf, this app gives you the tools to stay motivated and engaged.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">📚 Key Features</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 mb-4">
        <li>Track books you own, have read, or want to read</li>
        <li>Log reading status, star ratings, and reviews</li>
        <li>Filter and search by title, author, genre, or ownership</li>
        <li>Personalized stats and progress tracking</li>
        <li>Dark mode, keyboard shortcuts, and responsive design</li>
        <li>Optional notes, custom tags, and reading goals</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">🎯 Why It Exists</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        Unlike many commercial platforms, this app focuses on privacy and simplicity. There are no ads, no data sharing, and no clutter — just your books, your thoughts, and your progress.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">🔒 Your Data</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
        All of your data is stored privately and securely. No third-party APIs or trackers are used unless explicitly stated. Your reading journey stays yours.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">👋 Feedback & Suggestions</h2>
    <p>
        Got an idea to improve the app? Found a bug? Feel free to reach out via the Contact section or through the repository if this is an open-source project.
    </p>
</div>
